From 24046a4b66b300b5b6cde8d3dd817b17c553cd1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cat-s22 <>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:24:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] tt9-s22: keyboard threads at foreground-app priority; version 64.0-s22.3 (1650)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

system_server binds the IME without BIND_SCHEDULE_LIKE_TOP_APP while it is hidden,
so the process stays in the background group at nice 0 while the app being opened
runs at -10. When the keyboard hides, ActivityManager resets main to 0 and
RenderThread to -4, so the start of every input field (before it is shown) always
ran at low priority.

- ThreadPriority.boostUiThreads(): main and RenderThread to -10 (= TOP_APP_PRIORITY_BOOST)
  in onCreate, on every onStartInput, when shown and 0.5 s and 2 s after hiding.
- Maintenance tasks (persisting MindReader, saving pairs, normalizing) at
  THREAD_PRIORITY_BACKGROUND, then back to the previous priority of the pool thread.
